# The event sequences of TASK-02b (docs/research/task-02b/event-timelines.md)
# as scenarios in the POSIX session (TASK-21), then the hostile cases.
! panicked
! ZORAYA-PANIC
! ZORAYA-FAULT
! t_posix: FAIL
< PSURF>
# W9a: Ctrl-C during a parallel recursive build of three levels. The
# interrupt reaches every process of the foreground job at once; each leaf
# make deletes its partial target and re-raises; dash reports 130. The
# jobserver is make's FIFO in /tmp (the temporary service's FIFO nodes).
> cd /src/w9 && make -j8\r
< make[2]: Entering directory '/src/w9/b/2'
~ 2000 PSURF>
> \x03
< Deleting file 't4.h'
< Deleting file 't4.h'
< Deleting file 't4.h'
< Deleting file 't4.h'
< PSURF>
> echo status=$?; for d in a/1 a/2 b/1 b/2; do test -e $d/t4.h && echo left $d; done; echo checked\r
< status=130
< checked
x left
< PSURF>
# W9b: SIGTERM to the top make: it goes down the tree by make's own sends,
# each make deletes its partial target and re-raises; status 143. As measured
# (event-timelines.md), a leaf may not have begun its target when SIGTERM
# reaches it: three deletions at least, and no partial target left.
> make -j8 > /tmp/w9b.log 2>&1 & sleep 6; kill $!; wait $!; echo term=$?\r
< term=143
< PSURF>
> cat /tmp/w9b.log; for d in a/1 a/2 b/1 b/2; do test -e $d/t4.h && echo left $d; done; echo checked\r
< Deleting file 't4.h'
< Deleting file 't4.h'
< Deleting file 't4.h'
< checked
x left
< PSURF>
